<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Elvira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 305</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Synod of Elvira</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Elvira was a synod of the church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Roman Hispania</a> held at Iliberris (Elvira), near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, in the early 4th century, usually dated around 305. Its 81 canons, among the earliest surviving church laws, dealt with idolatry, marriage and relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and pagans, and required clerical continence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> and priests attended from across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, especially Baetica.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-elvira.jpg" alt="Council of Elvira" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jmdigne · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grenade,_Puerta_de_Elvira.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
